        "parms": "# array.map, filter, reduce and more — the functional family\nchord opens holding 60 64 67, oct 12 0 -12 and mel 48 60 55 72 65. Click the top-left button: chord sends its reference, which runs every object in the column below it.\nUnlike Max, these objects do not send each element out of a callback outlet and wait for the answer on an inlet. The work is an expression argument in .expr syntax: $i1 or $f1 is the element and $i2 its position. In array.reduce $i1 is the result so far and $i2 the element, and in array.tuplewise $i1 and $i2 are the elements of the two arrays. For a chain of objects per element, use array.iter, as the second row does.",
